<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26910" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŏcūtŭlēius</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>babbling, prating;</i> perh. only as <i>substt</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŏcū-tŭlēius</span></b> ,
				ii, m., <i>a talker,
				prater, babbler</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">veteres nostri hoc genus homines in verba
					projectos locutuleios et blaterones et lingulacas dixerunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 1, 15, 20</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŏcū-tŭlēĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f., <i>a female
				babbler</i>, = linguaculae, <i><span class="en">Non. 50,
			8</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
